# Reflection - Unit 3: Display Lists and Use Material Design

## What I Learned
- How to use data classes, functions, and collections in Kotlin.
- How to simulate scrollable lists and add click listeners.
- The principles of Material Design: colors, shapes, typography, and accessibility.

## Challenges
- Understanding how lists connect to UI components in Android.
- Translating Material Design guidelines into Kotlin-only simulations.
- Managing collections and filtering data efficiently.

## My Choices
- I used data classes to represent structured information (products).
- I simulated list scrolling and click listeners in Kotlin console output.
- I represented Material Design concepts with text-based simulations.

## Outcome
Unit 3 helped me connect Kotlin fundamentals with UI concepts.  
Even without Android Studio, I practiced the logic behind lists, click listeners, and design principles, preparing me for real Android UI development.
